# Rendering, local asset storage and the Edge TTS relay need no API key.
# Optional: enable real social dispatch through Buffer.
# Set in .env.local for development or Vercel's server environment, then restart/redeploy.
# NEVER prefix this key with VITE_ or paste it into the frontend.
BUFFER_API_KEY=

# Recommended: Vercel Blob as the one-time-configured upload host. Once connected,
# the app uploads every finished render itself and Buffer receives the permanent
# public link (https://<store>.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/…) — no manual link entry.
#
# Easiest on Vercel: Dashboard → Project → Storage → Blob → Create Store →
# "Connect" to this project. BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN is then injected automatically
# (redeploy afterwards). No VITE_ prefix!
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
#
# Alternative without any env: paste the Read/Write token once inside the app's
# dispatch window ("Vercel Blob verbinden"); it is stored in that browser only.
# A server-side token takes priority over the in-app token.
#
# Vercel Blob free tier (Hobby): 1 GB storage + 10 GB/month transfer — clean up
# old renders regularly (see README → "Upload-Host").
# Protect the deployment with authentication (see README); this is a private operator app.
# Qwen/Mistral keys remain optional and are configured in Machine Settings.
